«
@@ DMOTTest1 — demo of TTest1 when H₀ is true: ten values drawn from
@@ a normal law of mean 10 and standard deviation 1, tested against
@@ μ₀ = 10. H₀ is rejected at 5 % about one press in twenty, wrongly:
@@ that is what α means. Press again for a new sample.
@@ Author & design          : Jean Wilson
@@ Co-authors & programming  : Claude & Claude Code (Anthropic)
  10 0 0
  → dtn dt1 dt2
  «
    1 dtn For dti
      10 1 ⓁNormlRand
      Dup dt1 + 'dt1' Store Sq dt2 + 'dt2' Store
    Next
    dt1 dtn / dt2 dt1 Sq dtn / - dtn 1 - / √
    → dtm dts
    «
      dtm "mean" →Tag dts "s" →Tag
      dtn dtm dts 10 ⓁTTest1
      Dup DeleteTag 0.05 < "H₀ rejected at 5 %, wrongly" "H₀ kept" IFTE "verdict" →Tag
    »
  »
»
